.TH HSH 1 "August 2026" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple UNIX command interpreter.

It reads commands from the standard input and executes them.

The shell can be used in interactive mode or non-interactive mode.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
To start the shell in interactive mode:

.nf
./hsh
.fi

The shell displays a prompt and waits for the user to enter a command.

Example:

.nf
$ ./hsh
($) /bin/ls
($) exit
.fi

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
The shell can also receive commands through standard input.

Example:

.nf
echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
The shell returns an exit status depending on the result of the executed
command or internal operation.

.SH EXAMPLES
Run the shell:

.nf
./hsh
.fi

Execute a command:

.nf
($) /bin/ls
.fi

Run a command in non-interactive mode:

.nf
echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi

